with spikes a large metal ball floats in  istanbul's bus first straight  it's a sea mine built by the former  soviet union turkish commandos approach  it carefully the team will defuse the  device and then remove it  it's the second time in three days  turkish fishermen have found a mine like  this in their waters  last week russia's main intelligence  agency said 420 floating mines had  drifted into the black sea after  breaking up from cables near ukrainian  ports because of a storm ukraine denied  these claims it says russia planted the  mines  a former turkish rear admiral jihadi  says the tides and wind are diverting  the mines towards istanbul he believes  the mines belong to ukraine  it would be illogical for russia to mine  ports in odessa where it's aiming for a  military landing why would they shoot  themselves also if these mines broke off  so easily it means the mining wasn't  done properly that makes one think the  mines were left to float free in the  black sea  international law allows states to lay  sea mines in their waters to protect  themselves from attack but allowing  mines to float into international waters  is illegal  the u.n should be questioning ukraine  turkey has a strong capacity to sweep  the mines but this is an irresponsible  act  no matter who was responsible for the  mines they now pose a serious risk to  local fishermen like shaheen who have  been told not to fish at night  shahin says when turkey diffused the  mines in the sea last week the explosion  hit like an earthquake  if you don't see the mine then you  explode you're done only a slight  contact is enough to do it night fishing  is banned now thank god it's the end of  the season but if we were in peak season  then the scenario would be different  we're expecting many more mines to drift  by here in a month or so  the black sea is a major shipping artery  for grain oil and oil products turkish  trades are the only waterways trying it  to the mediterranean and the asian seas  38 000 vessels passed through the strait  of istanbul last year any interruption  or risk in this region could disrupt the  global supply chain  at this time it is not clear who is  responsible for these mines or how many  of them are floating out there posing a  threat to people and marine life unless  these questions are answered it may take  years to spot and disable these  explosive devices in the black sea sinam  kyo solo al jazeera istanbul
 

